    "fixed_outcome": "Both before/after-apply caught panics prevent continued GC; recovery preserves the input and the original request result",
    "source_binding": "Baseline and current tests use isolated Cargo target directories. An earlier shared-target attempt unexpectedly passed and is excluded from evidence; final baseline sources match the frozen checkpoint and both sides use the same regression source."
  },
  "scope": "Actual generic commit effect dispatch and guard placement, checked against per-transaction lower-effect contracts. Finite interruption/recovery/retirement and application-level training-checkpoint models, plus real installed-package restart/GC regressions.",
  "remaining": "Native CommitIo conformance, complete roots/closures, lower catalog/Journal/application meaning, multi-request protocol/GC refinement and full conditional progress remain open. Verus does not verify Rust unwinding. Real sampler/trainer integration and external model/optimizer/RNG checkpoint selection/publication are not verified or automatically implemented.",
  "verus_positive_checks": 272,
  "targeted_verus_negative_cases": 14,
  "tlc_cases": 22,
  "native_tests": 63,
  "python_tests": 888,
  "check_scope": "Full positive Verus plus nine algorithm and five effect-contract negative controls; 13 positive and nine negative TLC cases for the two new models; isolated native tests and full installed-wheel Python tests, examples, protocol/WAL campaigns, default/Python Clippy and Rust/Python formatting. No fresh full older-negative/TLC campaign is claimed.",
  "resume_findings": {
    "sampling": "Three abrupt subprocess-exit cases recover the last committed continuation, reject stale attempts and preserve idempotent completion. A published but unsaved continuation is not adopted. Active lease interruption consumes the existing retry budget.",
    "training": "Online GC reclaims post-checkpoint processed results without replay ownership; restoring the older consumer cursor is then rejected before WAL change. Explicit replay ownership permits matching checkpoint restoration and mock-optimizer replay, including release of the extra owner after queue ownership is restored.",
    "boundary": "Queue WAL recovery returns the latest consumer state, which can be ahead of an external model checkpoint. Application-managed checkpoint selection, consistent tokens/RNG and post-checkpoint replay ownership remain required; these tests are not a real training-framework end-to-end proof."
  },
